# Example dist-git `sources` file.
#
# Copy this to the repository ROOT as `sources` (no extension) and replace the
# entry below with your real tarball's checksum.
#
# Format (one source per line, BSD `shaNsum --tag` style):
#   HASHTYPE (filename) = hexdigest
#
# - HASHTYPE : SHA512 (preferred) or SHA256.
# - filename : must match the Source0:/SourceN: filename in your .spec.
# - hexdigest: checksum of the tarball.
#
# Generate the line with:
#   sha512sum --tag mypackage-1.0.tar.gz >> sources
#
# The tarball itself is NOT committed. On build, the workflow looks it up in the
# lookaside cache by this checksum; on a miss it downloads the matching
# Source URL from your spec, verifies this checksum, and caches it back.
#
SHA512 (mypackage-1.0.tar.gz) = REPLACE_ME_WITH_THE_REAL_SHA512_OF_YOUR_TARBALL
